"# Petstore

> A sample API.

Version 2.0.0 — OpenAPI 3.1.0.

Base URL: https://api.example.com/v1

Authentication: bearerAuth: http/bearer, apiKeyAuth: apiKey.

## Guides

- [Getting started](https://docs.example.com/api/index.html#/page/getting-started)

## Concepts

- [Pagination](https://docs.example.com/api/index.html#/page/pagination)

## Workflows

- [Create a pet](https://docs.example.com/api/index.html#/scenario/create-pet): 2 steps, 2 inputs
- [Find a pet](https://docs.example.com/api/index.html#/scenario/find-a-pet): 1 step, 1 input — the [Arazzo recipe](https://docs.example.com/workflows/search.arazzo.yaml) runs it unchanged in CI.

## pets

- [GET /pets](https://docs.example.com/api/index.html#/op/listPets): List pets
- [POST /pets](https://docs.example.com/api/index.html#/op/createPet): Create a pet

## search

- [GET /search](https://docs.example.com/api/index.html#/op/legacySearch): (deprecated) Search everything

## Other operations

- [GET /ping](https://docs.example.com/api/index.html#/op/ping): Liveness probe.

## Webhooks

- [POST petAdopted](https://docs.example.com/api/index.html#/op/webhook-post-petadopted): Pet adopted

## Reference

- [Full documentation (llms-full.txt)](https://docs.example.com/api/llms-full.txt): every operation with its parameters, schemas and examples
- [OpenAPI specification](https://api.example.com/openapi.json): the machine-readable contract

## Optional

- [Status page](https://status.example.com)
